@title what answers a verb, and the staff channel

  cominfo
  cominfo <verb>
  cominfo <verb> <player>

Every verb the player can type, where it comes from and whether the
function behind it exists. Each line reads

  decir /lib/player->do_say() found in /lib/living/communicate.

"not found" means the action is registered on a function nobody
defines: the verb exists and can never work.

With no argument it lists everything, actions first and then the
files under /lib/cmds the player may reach. With a verb it shows
only that one, and with a player's name it asks about that player
instead of you.

  coders <message>

The staff channel. It takes the same options every channel does:
'?' for them, '!' for the last messages, '.' for who is listening,
and 'on' and 'off'.
